{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:29:03Z","created_by_operation":"op_b6caac6861924643a8bd47ba966d7dd2","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_1b96dcc960e23365e78bfc048dadbbd7658a1304e0aded762729ca85b7e5dd50","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=components","setting":"pardesco/hypernovum@e6469da5b680 snapshot be1c689a4163012b","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_6b46bf5123f5fef0ba0743c7bc1b556c3fde88526af7bda4ff443347f515c425","slc_92ae33c63617d033eb93ff2e774fd61ee6290826d87f54dfd06b279853775717","slc_e16ee3ea94a2db331b675c3e74b1d2e0313f62d4344e7036c0da09050a19ad2a"],"source_ids":["src_ab1f4787350d59339190b7e30439b8b5"],"text":"The city visualization includes a bin-packed district layout, seven procedural silhouette families, a cyberpunk shader system with bloom, CSS2D labels, hover tooltips, a central Neural Core geodesic sphere, and animated Data Arteries on file changes.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:29:03Z","updated_by_operation":"op_b6caac6861924643a8bd47ba966d7dd2"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:29:03Z","created_by_operation":"op_b6caac6861924643a8bd47ba966d7dd2","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_200b366b3b1999a3f37be5fe40c7d50d6e12a10dfd30aa37062359155289297f","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=interfaces","setting":"pardesco/hypernovum@e6469da5b680 snapshot be1c689a4163012b","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_67fe1f057d78e2e38357ce7bf1b164a0c44ea1c7c344caf813ba9588fcf5084b","slc_9cb032d99db1f77764be081db7da1ecdd1cba8a0a222bbcd8a79366843da95fa","slc_9cd5c00976c1400e8b4c98672a7fb3b566155112993500bfae8116ed9915f0ab","slc_e6d4f38426786e7b02143db9a1143fd0d0d8cd8b2e080891cac697b3d61e685c"],"source_ids":["src_ab1f4787350d59339190b7e30439b8b5"],"text":"The heartbeat script is invoked as node <vault>/.hypernovum/heartbeat.js with --vault plus either --hook (reading session_id, tool_name and cwd from stdin JSON) or explicit --id/--name/--state/--file flags, and --stop to finish a session.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:29:03Z","updated_by_operation":"op_b6caac6861924643a8bd47ba966d7dd2"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:29:03Z","created_by_operation":"op_b6caac6861924643a8bd47ba966d7dd2","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_2806e6686436aa0a2edcdd29f1a1381c1ddf24c2a295291fcf6a2494a4450017","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=components","setting":"pardesco/hypernovum@e6469da5b680 snapshot be1c689a4163012b","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_03bb69b8f2c033c22078c92100c7a22f5f266427d3a34b401999f5e71ed4ab3a"],"source_ids":["src_ab1f4787350d59339190b7e30439b8b5"],"text":"Agent integration includes an Activity Monitor polling per-session snapshots in .hypernovum/agents/, a terminal launcher for Claude Code, GPT Codex, Antigravity CLI or a custom command, and a SETUP.md context handoff written before launch.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:29:03Z","updated_by_operation":"op_b6caac6861924643a8bd47ba966d7dd2"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:29:03Z","created_by_operation":"op_b6caac6861924643a8bd47ba966d7dd2","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_366b2bfdb4ebb46d796b737808f956301b20c4d16e8a653d8430c69829b16d02","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=interfaces","setting":"pardesco/hypernovum@e6469da5b680 snapshot be1c689a4163012b","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_10b3840c2fb47d7ff29bfe20ca39ee1ab4fd30b1a4e3a0bad48a6ddeea373f35","slc_f5bb6ad950f3b0c50b1f7118f8f9e892b6f593b783e389c39ee275c4cde7ce00"],"source_ids":["src_ab1f4787350d59339190b7e30439b8b5"],"text":"The plugin exposes an 'Open code city' command-palette command and a ribbon cube; the city view supports single-click select/focus, double-click to open the note, right-click menus, search/filters, scan lenses, lens presets, and EDGES chips.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:29:03Z","updated_by_operation":"op_b6caac6861924643a8bd47ba966d7dd2"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:29:03Z","created_by_operation":"op_b6caac6861924643a8bd47ba966d7dd2","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_505d8f63fec9079e5484f9bfa60ce49193e1f3c6df85502174c7c56977f80bc3","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=design-choices","setting":"pardesco/hypernovum@e6469da5b680 snapshot be1c689a4163012b","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_16ed8ae336367aeb6059cf84ac3c894a96c07bd375a6523de5a7c46867db3f0e","slc_4c74a8ee310218490f349ff6e0b581ad9f4c286c1d394549fa4ee88e91aec04a"],"source_ids":["src_ab1f4787350d59339190b7e30439b8b5","src_e95dbe2419565169aa952334f24398ed"],"text":"An untagged vault renders as a whole-vault fallback (folders as districts, notes as buildings, height from incoming links); tagging one note switches the city to project mode, and the fallback only applies at zero projects.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:29:03Z","updated_by_operation":"op_b6caac6861924643a8bd47ba966d7dd2"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:29:03Z","created_by_operation":"op_b6caac6861924643a8bd47ba966d7dd2","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_8686c668cbc29dea2fced77cdae51b5ef3650dbbab2b6a326fda929cc079d8da","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=specifications","setting":"pardesco/hypernovum@e6469da5b680 snapshot be1c689a4163012b","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_4fbf1106886c942aa36e595d11be54e80b9f4f02a901f83f72484c5691de8c33","slc_acfde591d79ff44f1d523c47173ae2d43e76670a1651a84bfc634a4208f71a93","slc_b5e64cbdf4479adb1fdb1361a0923840669b23e2f520d613cebc11222259d622"],"source_ids":["src_ab1f4787350d59339190b7e30439b8b5"],"text":"Projects are detected by a frontmatter tag 'project' or 'type: project' (tag configurable in settings), with fields including status, priority, category, stack, tasks, questions, depends_on, blocked_by and projectDir.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:29:03Z","updated_by_operation":"op_b6caac6861924643a8bd47ba966d7dd2"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:29:03Z","created_by_operation":"op_b6caac6861924643a8bd47ba966d7dd2","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_98b4bf59fe92ee7111c8c22afeff2b9e362d39a71c879635b0aac74fce151282","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=dependencies","setting":"pardesco/hypernovum@e6469da5b680 snapshot be1c689a4163012b","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_73971de0e0787db1b15e3d3b96d2399528ec7eb7e719a87165e9b680f8b26aac","slc_a0e9b30ddd90955786b66ea9c7615c0d0a99fd78f58106991eff01112ffcf581"],"source_ids":["src_ab1f4787350d59339190b7e30439b8b5","src_e95dbe2419565169aa952334f24398ed"],"text":"The plugin is built with Three.js, Zustand, and the Obsidian Plugin API, and requires Obsidian minAppVersion 1.6.0.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:29:03Z","updated_by_operation":"op_b6caac6861924643a8bd47ba966d7dd2"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:29:03Z","created_by_operation":"op_b6caac6861924643a8bd47ba966d7dd2","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_ab340a9235558648930a5dee7f95863068977816f6789a64433067ac7dae5d26","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=tools-permissions","setting":"pardesco/hypernovum@e6469da5b680 snapshot be1c689a4163012b","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_4c4355a9ee51cd722ea4b3ff54bf982bc61a18876ea1cabee9d5023881d763f5","slc_bd76f0d2c59e543e52de042d58a178246f4c416bf440c8f1e3834fd3c83b905f"],"source_ids":["src_ab1f4787350d59339190b7e30439b8b5"],"text":"The plugin makes no network requests of any kind; all reads and writes are local. It runs read-only git commands in projectDir-linked folders, opens terminals only on explicit Launch agent clicks, and never reads the clipboard.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:29:03Z","updated_by_operation":"op_b6caac6861924643a8bd47ba966d7dd2"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:29:03Z","created_by_operation":"op_b6caac6861924643a8bd47ba966d7dd2","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_ba216a48a59ed43f4c54b99667f3b94b94dc87032a86a988ee362ba5b09b3ea7","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=workflows","setting":"pardesco/hypernovum@e6469da5b680 snapshot be1c689a4163012b","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_6021dcabef26419a16335b9d7708efd4cc56f5d103975373c30216641d185e69","slc_664ad87a5d571b9101dc3bc829007daef1a5f57cc25ef65b514b1303e7269200","slc_7982c99936b403d4db25404b208a58f6e9e3a0635dbdf03e822efe7ab0dc58ce"],"source_ids":["src_ab1f4787350d59339190b7e30439b8b5","src_e95dbe2419565169aa952334f24398ed"],"text":"Repository development practice: development uses npm scripts (dev, build, typecheck, vitest tests), releases are cut from the root manifest.json with check-versions.mjs mirroring versions, and CI typechecks and tests before building.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:29:03Z","updated_by_operation":"op_b6caac6861924643a8bd47ba966d7dd2"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:29:03Z","created_by_operation":"op_b6caac6861924643a8bd47ba966d7dd2","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_f8b30caa3c027d50fb9e8777ae1a91683ce5261ae48862a81728f6730b10ffb5","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=memory-state","setting":"pardesco/hypernovum@e6469da5b680 snapshot be1c689a4163012b","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_dc751b1c5b885954864198541aa7ba2810d242818ab95dfd7d35158fbaf5b09f"],"source_ids":["src_ab1f4787350d59339190b7e30439b8b5"],"text":"Heartbeat v2 writes one snapshot file per session (.hypernovum/agents/<sessionId>.json) so concurrent agents don't clobber each other; orbs are colored by state and overlapping --file values on one project surface a deterministic conflict.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:29:03Z","updated_by_operation":"op_b6caac6861924643a8bd47ba966d7dd2"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:29:03Z","created_by_operation":"op_b6caac6861924643a8bd47ba966d7dd2","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_ff6067f92da0b04d90126e2cbaf7c510913d9e7f3005d2af7efbba900a6b2383","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=tools-permissions","setting":"pardesco/hypernovum@e6469da5b680 snapshot be1c689a4163012b","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_725d3a23e89df4c8d6be6a006eef20cf37bf86bfa8d1782fcbf5d61b30b435d7","slc_a0e9b30ddd90955786b66ea9c7615c0d0a99fd78f58106991eff01112ffcf581"],"source_ids":["src_ab1f4787350d59339190b7e30439b8b5","src_e95dbe2419565169aa952334f24398ed"],"text":"A vault mode turns the entire agent layer off — no process execution and no reads outside the vault — while the city, lenses, filters and backlink graph keep working; first run asks whether to enable the agent layer.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:29:03Z","updated_by_operation":"op_b6caac6861924643a8bd47ba966d7dd2"}
